    "body": "Controlled P1-V03 / V2-P1-04 test completed. CLOSED WITHOUT MERGING.\n\nNegative head: 5c8b52d606f25d807e97029f0c80d48762af165c; base main: f9df7a30747aba111ee7df0afe209fd613cae869.\n[Negative run 45674710740](https://github.com/ManeaAlShabrain/QASCP/actions/runs/45674710740) failed Foundation verification and QASCP Foundation Gate because README.md referenced missing-controlled-main-enforcement-probe.md. Downstream full-validator/test steps were skipped, not passed.\n\nWhile this PR was OPEN, NON-DRAFT and targeting main at that negative head, REST reported mergeable=true (no content conflict), mergeable_state=blocked and merged=false. The required failed check was produced by github-actions, App ID 15368. Active ruleset 27321554 required that exact check with strict updates and no bypass actors. No merge request was submitted and no override was attempted.\n\nPositive control: commit 2ffc0a864c3d7cf9b43041dadfaffa1bf2438438 restored the exact baseline tree 2c21d99bdeb0a1773a35c9fe53dbf4969854b5b7, without any rule/workflow change. [Positive run 45674930080](https://github.com/ManeaAlShabrain/QASCP/actions/runs/45674930080) passed both foundation and gate. The restored PR has zero net changed files.\n\nThis isolates required-check enforcement from draft state or missing approvals. It is configuration plus an observed blocked merge state, not an executed merge-endpoint rejection or universal proof for future settings.\n\nReview bundle: #36. That bundle has its own 96-test candidate evidence. Phase approval and independent security/architecture/bilingual/regulatory decisions remain separate."
